  "changes": [
    "Reuse one independently owned immutable-byte/decoder implementation for initial publication and resident reopen.",
    "Copy artifacts up to 256 KiB under a transient logical read pin; reserve memory first and retain provider/resource ownership across Store close. Size or optional residency refusal retains range-source fallback.",
    "Small reopen creates no durable artifact alias, marker, native extent lease or checkpoint-wide pin. Operational errors remain authoritative.",
    "Already completed physical retirement does not stage missing tombstones or advance checkpoints.",
    "Integrity inspection checks proof images even with a durability witness, reports structural corruption, propagates cancellation/operational failures, and restores the borrowed cancellation token.",
    "Private sequence rebinding rejects an inherited active proof rather than invalidating its authenticated sequence."
  ],
